# .forge-format — per-project formatter override for the forge pre-commit gate.
#
# To activate: copy this file to `.forge-format` at your repo root, then put ONE
# line below naming the formatter command (binary + flags ONLY). forge appends
# the staged file paths for you — do NOT add file arguments or shell operators; the
# line is parsed as argv and run directly (never eval'd), so `;`, `|`, command
# substitution are inert.
#
# The first word must be an allowed formatter binary. Default allowlist:
#   prettier black ruff isort yapf autopep8 gofmt rustfmt cargo clang-format
#   shfmt dprint eslint taplo ktlint swiftformat php-cs-fixer yamlfmt
# Permit another binary with: FORGE_FORMAT_ALLOW=mytool git commit  (colon-sep).
#
# Examples (one line, no file args — forge appends the staged paths):
#
#   prettier --write
#   black
#   ruff format
#   gofmt -w
#   rustfmt
#   clang-format -i
#
# Leave this file as `.forge-format.example` (inert) if auto-detection already
# picks the right formatter — see docs/formatting.md for the detection order.
#
# --- put your one-line formatter command below this line ---
